---
import RelayDiagram from "./RelayDiagram.tsx";
---

<section id="private" class="night" aria-labelledby="private-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="private-title">
      Draw together.
      <br />
      Nobody in between can read it.
    </h2>
    <p class="lede">
      When you share a drawing, your browser makes a key and puts it in the link. Everything you
      draw is locked with that key before it leaves your computer, so the relay that passes it along
      and the copy kept online only ever hold scrambled bytes.
    </p>

    <figure class="together">
      <video
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        poster="/media/crowd.webp"
        aria-label="Six browsers on one drawing, side by side, each named: whatever one person adds appears in the other five as it is drawn"
        data-inview
      >
        <source src="/media/crowd.webm" type="video/webm" />
        <source src="/media/crowd.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption>
        Six browsers on one drawing, recorded as it happened (the film on it is{" "}
        <i>Big Buck Bunny</i> © Blender Foundation,{" "}
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/">CC BY 3.0</a>). Underneath, this is
        what travels:
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="diagram">
      <RelayDiagram client:visible />
    </div>

    <figure class="link" aria-labelledby="link-caption">
      <div class="url">
        <span class="part sent">app.hydrawn.eu.org/boards/k7vq2m9xh3tqbw4ne8rj5c6dpa</span>
        <span class="part kept">#room=Qm9yZGVyc2VhbF9rZXlfZXhhbXBsZV8zMmJ5dGVz</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="link-caption" class="legend">
        <span class="sent-note">
          <b>Sent to the server:</b> which drawing.
        </span>
        <span class="kept-note">
          <b>Never sent:</b> the key. Browsers keep what follows the # to themselves.
        </span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <dl class="facts">
      <div>
        <dt>The key travels in the link</dt>
        <dd>
          Anyone you send the link to can open the drawing. Nobody else can, the server included.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Locked before it leaves</dt>
        <dd>
          Each stroke is sealed with AES-256-GCM in your browser. The relay forwards bytes it cannot
          open.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Still there after you leave</dt>
        <dd>
          An encrypted copy stays online, so the link keeps working when you close the tab. It is
          deleted after a year without edits.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .night {
    background-color: var(--night);
    background-image: radial-gradient(
      circle at 1px 1px,
      rgb(236 235 248 / 0.09) 1.1px,
      transparent 0
    );
    background-size: 22px 22px;
    color: var(--night-ink);
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 10vw, 128px);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    max-width: 58ch;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--night-soft);
  }

  .together {
    margin: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px) 0 0;
  }
  .together video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1920 / 800;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #e3e2ee;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.8);
  }
  .together figcaption {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--highlight);
  }

  .diagram {
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px);
  }

  .link {
    margin: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px) 0 0;
  }
  /* Wraps rather than scrolls: a scrolling box would need to take the keyboard focus. */
  .url {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #0f0e20;
    border: 1px solid rgb(236 235 248 / 0.12);
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: clamp(0.8125rem, 1.6vw, 1rem);
  }
  .part {
    padding: 2px 0;
  }
  .sent {
    color: var(--night-soft);
  }
  .kept {
    color: var(--night);
    background: var(--highlight);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding-inline: 4px;
  }
  .legend {
    margin-top: 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px 32px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--night-soft);
  }
  .legend b {
    color: var(--night-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .kept-note b {
    color: var(--highlight);
  }

  .facts {
    margin: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 28px clamp(24px, 4vw, 56px);
  }
  .facts div {
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(236 235 248 / 0.16);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: var(--night-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
